#
# ==========================================================================
# STATE / TERRITORY LAYER (subdivisions)
# ==========================================================================
# All 50 states + DC and the five territories (AS, GU, MP, PR, VI) are the ISO
# 3166-2:US checklist (57 subdivisions). North Dakota (US-ND) and the US Minor
# Outlying Islands (US-UM) observe only the federal set, so they carry no
# beyond-federal rows -- honest silence, not an omission.
#
# SCOPE: each subdivision's holidays that fall BEYOND the federal set (a
# distinct date, or a state-renamed observance the state fixes by its own
# statute). Same-date federal renames (a state's "Presidents' Day" for the
# federal Washington's Birthday) are carried too, as the state's own named
# rule. Weekend in-lieu "(observed)" days are NOT modelled here: whether a
# state grants the Friday-before / Monday-after varies by employer and year,
# and the nominal statutory date is the firm datum -- future data.
#
# SOURCES: the distinctive holidays are grounded in each state's own government
# page (primary), cross-checked one-for-one against vacanza/holidays 0.101
# (MIT) for the 57-subdivision checklist and the long-tail dates. Primary
# state citations for the twenty most distinctive:
#   Texas Independence Day / San Jacinto Day / Confederate Memorial Day (Jan 19)
#     / LBJ Day / Emancipation Day in Texas -- Texas Gov't Code sec. 662.003
#     (statutory & optional holidays), https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/GV/htm/GV.662.htm
#   Patriots' Day (MA) -- Mass. Gen. Laws ch.6 sec.12J, https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleI/Chapter6/Section12J
#   Patriots' Day (ME) -- Maine Rev. Stat. tit.1 sec.1051, https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/1/title1sec1051.html
#   Pioneer Day (UT) -- Utah Code sec.63G-1-301, https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title63G/Chapter1/63G-1-S301.html
#   Cesar Chavez Day (CA) -- Cal. Gov't Code sec.6700, https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?sectionNum=6700&lawCode=GOV
#   Mardi Gras (LA) -- La. Rev. Stat. sec.1:55, https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=321848
#   Nevada Day (NV) -- Nev. Rev. Stat. sec.236.015, https://www.leg.state.nv.us/nrs/nrs-236.html
#   Seward's Day / Alaska Day (AK) -- Alaska Stat. sec.44.12.010, http://www.akleg.gov/basis/statutes.asp#44.12.010
#   Kamehameha Day / Prince Kuhio Day / Statehood Day (HI) -- Haw. Rev. Stat. sec.8-1..8-5, https://www.capitol.hawaii.gov/hrscurrent/Vol01_Ch0001-0042F/HRS0008/
#   West Virginia Day (WV) -- W.Va. Code sec.2-2-1, https://code.wvlegislature.gov/2-2-1/
#   Truman Day (MO) -- Mo. Rev. Stat. sec.9.010, https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=9.010
#   Emancipation Day (DC) -- DC Official Code sec.1-612.02, https://code.dccouncil.gov/us/dc/council/code/sections/1-612.02
#   Bennington Battle Day / Town Meeting Day (VT) -- 1 V.S.A. sec.371, https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/01/007/00371
#   Casimir Pulaski Day (IL) -- 5 ILCS 490/65, https://www.ilga.gov/legislation/ilcs/ilcs4.asp?ActID=176
#   Confederate Memorial Day / Jefferson Davis Birthday (AL) -- Ala. Code sec.1-3-8, https://law.justia.com/codes/alabama/title-1/chapter-3/section-1-3-8/
#   Arbor Day (NE) -- Neb. Rev. Stat. sec.25-2221, https://nebraskalegislature.gov/laws/statutes.php?statute=25-2221
#   Puerto Rico Constitution Day / Emancipation Day (PR) -- 1 LPRA sec.71
#   Guam Discovery Day / Liberation Day (GU) -- 1 GCA sec.1000
#   American Samoa Flag Day (AS) -- ASCA sec.1.0501
#   Victory Day (RI) -- R.I. Gen. Laws sec.25-1-1, http://webserver.rilegislature.gov/Statutes/TITLE25/25-1/25-1-1.HTM
# REFERENCE-ATTRIBUTED ROWS (vacanza/holidays 0.101, MIT -- no readily citable
# standalone primary page found, so the date is taken from the reference and
# marked here): all remaining long-tail subdivision rows (the federal-rename
# "Presidents'/Washington/Lincoln" third-Monday variants; "Day/Friday After
# Thanksgiving" and its named cousins State Holiday GA / Family Day NV / Native
# American Heritage Day WA / American Indian Heritage Day MD; Christmas Eve /
# New Year's Eve / Day After Christmas full-day state closures KS/MI/NC/TX/WI;
# Good Friday state closures; Election Day; the CNMI/Guam/Virgin-Islands
# territorial observances; Frances Xavier Cabrini Day CO; Susan B. Anthony Day).
#
# Election Day is modelled as a biennial decree (even-year general election,
# the Tuesday after the first Monday of November) for states that observe it
# only in general-election years, and as an every-year nth_weekday rule for
# Indiana and New York, which the reference lists in odd years too.
